<!-- anchor:enum-column-vocab -->
**Fixed vocabulary (enum columns)**
- `Result` : Success / Failure / Partial
- `Conclusion` : Continue / Pivot / Discarded
- `Status` : To Do / In Progress / Blocked / On Hold / Done / Canceled ← `01_exploration_tree.md` only. A computed value that a person does not choose. Status determination → grep -F "anchor:status-determination" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
- `Distance to destination` : Closer / Same / Farther ← session file CHECK only
- `Validity` : Valid / Invalid ← `02_knowledge_base.md` lesson index only. A **separate column** from `Status`
- The order of the values in each vocabulary is fixed. `nav.js` reads the values by order. Do not add values or change the order.
<!-- anchor-end:enum-column-vocab -->

<!-- anchor:composite-why-closest -->
**Composite column grammar — `Why closest`**
```
Why closest:  D1, D2 met / D3 unmet — {prose on why it was close}
```
- ID span regex: `^({Destination criterion PK}(, {Destination criterion PK})* met|None met)( / {Destination criterion PK}(, {Destination criterion PK})* unmet)?$` ({Destination criterion PK} → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS))
- Prose span: must not be blank. It is a **no-compression target**, so it is not summarized or deleted.
<!-- anchor-end:composite-why-closest -->

<!-- anchor:composite-invalidation -->
**Composite column grammar — `Invalidation`** (`knowledge/K###.md`)
```
Invalidation:    None
Invalidation:    2026-07-18 — returning to #4 made the fixed-driver premise itself no longer hold
```
- There are **only two allowed forms**: `None` or `{Session PK} — {prose}`. `—` (unfilled) is a **violation**
- ID span regex: `^{Session PK}$` — **one** session PK, the session where the return was recorded ({Session PK} → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS))
- Prose span: must not be blank. It is a **no-compression target**, so it is not summarized or deleted
- The return span (`#7`·`#4`) is not written here. Which return it was is joined by the session PK (the `Body` column of the Return Log has the same date)
- ※ `Invalidated lessons` in `01_exploration_tree.md` is a **different column (an ID column)**.
  Key matching is done by **exact match** — with partial matching, `Invalidation` would also catch `Invalidated lessons`
<!-- anchor-end:composite-invalidation -->

<!-- anchor:composite-in-effect -->
**Composite column grammar — `In effect`** (`00_destination.md`)
```
In effect: Valid
In effect: Discarded — 2026-07-19, this criterion became unnecessary after the higher goal changed
```
- There are **only two allowed forms**: `Valid` (a single token) or `Discarded — {Date literal}, {prose}`. `—` (unfilled) is a **violation**
- Value regex (exact match): `^Valid$` passes / anything else must match `^Discarded — {Date literal}, .+$` to pass ({Date literal} → grep -F "anchor:date-literal-full-list" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS))
- The left keyword is only `Valid`/`Discarded`, and this column regex enforces it — **it is not put in the fixed vocabulary list of enum columns**
  (if it were, I-05 would also treat this column as an enum column and collide with the composite check. The same trap as the `Status`/`Validity` split)
- `{date}` is a **calendar date literal** `YYYY-MM-DD`. It is neither a session PK nor an FK (audit log)
- `{prose}` (reason for discarding): must not be blank. It is a **no-compression target**, so it is not summarized or deleted
- This column sits on a **separate line** from the `D#` row (directly below the D#)
<!-- anchor-end:composite-in-effect -->

