<!-- anchor:notation-grammar -->
**Notation grammar (common to all files)**

| Item | Rule |
|---|---|
| Multi-value separator | `, ` (comma + space) fixed. `/`, `·` and line breaks forbidden |
| Multi-value ordering | **Ascending, fixed** (`#K002, #K005`). Stabilizes diffs and invariant comparison |
| Ordered ID list | ★ `Path:` is the **only exception.** Separator ` → ` (space on both sides) fixed, **sorting forbidden** (the order is the meaning) |
| Checked, not applicable | `None` |
| Unfilled / template initial value | `—` (em dash) |
| Parenthesized note after an ID | **Forbidden**. `#K003 (driver)` → `#K003`. The only exception is `Discovered:` in `knowledge/K###.md` |
| Attempt PK search pattern | `#7\b` — without `\b`, `#70` is a false hit |
| Order of table data rows | Older rows on top; a new row is added at the **very bottom** of the table. "Latest row" = the bottom data row. Migration starts from the **top** data row |
| Template row | A row whose cells are all `—` is not a data row (excluded from row counts and format checks). It is replaced when the first data row is written |
| Initial values before first wrap | In `01_exploration_tree.md`, frontmatter `last_updated` and ★ `Started:` start as `YYYY-MM-DD`, and ★ `Body:` starts as `sessions/YYYY-MM-DD.md`. While `last_updated` is `YYYY-MM-DD` (before the first `/pdca-wrap` that ends a cycle writes), all three values must be these initial values to pass the format check, and the existence of the ★ `Body:` file is not checked |

- `Discovered:` test: `^{Attempt PK} \({Date literal}\)$` **exact match** ({Attempt PK} → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS), {Date literal} → grep -F "anchor:date-literal-full-list" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS))
  (`#7 (driver issue)` → violation, `#7 (2026-07-20)` → pass)
<!-- anchor-end:notation-grammar -->

