## ② Branching · Current position

<!-- anchor:branch-point-value-rule -->
**`Branch point` value rule** (Recent Attempts · Discarded Directions · Migrated Attempt Summaries)

`Branch point` = the attempt PK of the point this attempt branched out from. When writing a new row, use the value of the first true row of the table below, from the top.

| Order | Condition | Value |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | The `#` of this row is `#0` | `—` |
| 2 | An attempt that ran a next direction candidate, or a candidate discarded without running | Copy the `Branch point:` value of that candidate as it is |
| 3 | Otherwise | The ★ `Attempt #:` value right before writing this row |

- Value format: {Attempt PK} or `—` (condition 1 only). `None` and blank are violations. {Attempt PK} → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
- In the Discarded Directions table `Branch point` is required even in a row whose `#` is `—` (`—` forbidden).
- On migration the `Branch point` value is moved as it is.
<!-- anchor-end:branch-point-value-rule -->

<!-- anchor:current-position-update -->
**★ Current Position update rule** (the tree write of `/pdca-wrap`)

Return = writing a new Return Log row in this cycle. P = the attempt PK of this cycle. B = the `Branch point` value of the P row.

| Field | When returned | When not returned |
|---|---|---|
| `Attempt #:` | The PK of the return point | P |
| `Path:` | The existing path cut at the return point node (return point included) | Unchanged if the end node is P. If B is a node of the existing path, the existing path cut at the B node (B included) with P appended. Otherwise the chain path of B with P appended |
| `Direction:` | One line of prose confirmed by the user | One line of prose confirmed by the user |
| `Status:` | The computed status of the new `Attempt #:` value set by this table | The computed status of the new `Attempt #:` value set by this table |
| `Started:` | Today | Today if `Attempt #:` changed, otherwise unchanged |
| `Body:` | The session file path of this cycle | The session file path of this cycle if `Attempt #:` changed, otherwise unchanged |

- Pre-write condition: when returned = the return point is a node of the existing path. When not returned = the end node of the existing path is P, or B is a node of the existing path, or the chain path of B is not `None`. B when the P row does not exist yet = the `Branch point` value to be written in that row. Chain path = the `ChainPath:` value of the `node .claude/hooks/nav.js onpath {B}` output.
- At the step that receives whether a return happened, `/pdca-wrap` tests the pre-write condition with the `EndNode:` · `Contains:` · `RowBranchPoint:` · `ChainPath:` values of the `node .claude/hooks/nav.js onpath {Attempt PK}` output. If false, it writes nothing and asks again whether a return happened.
- Path format → grep -F "anchor:01-format-position-path-attempt" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS) · Status determination → grep -F "anchor:status-determination" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
- `Status:` is not chosen by a person. Copy the `Status:` value of the `node .claude/hooks/nav.js state {new Attempt #}` output as it is.
- A span abandoned by a return is not written in the path. The trace of a return is kept only in the Return Log table. When an attempt of an abandoned span is resumed and the path is written from its chain path, that span comes back into the path.
<!-- anchor-end:current-position-update -->

<!-- anchor:status-determination -->
**Status · Result determination** (computed values — `nav.js` computes them from the session files. A person does not choose them)

- Round = from a round header of a session file to right before the next `## ` line. Closed round = a round whose `Conclusion:` line is a conclusion word. Open round = any other round.
- Rounds of attempt X = the rounds in all session files whose header attempt number is X. Order = ascending file date, and top to bottom inside one file.
- Latest closed round = the last in that order among the closed rounds of attempt X.

**Result** (the value of one round) = computed from the item lines (starting with `- [`) that follow directly below the CHECK `Success criteria met:` line of that round. The first true row from the top.

| Order | Condition | Result |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | There are 0 item lines, or there is an item line that does not fit the format | Undetermined |
| 2 | All item lines are `[x]` | Success |
| 3 | All item lines are `[ ]` | Failure |
| 4 | Otherwise | Partial |

**Status** (the value of attempt X). The first true row from the top.

| Order | Condition | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | X has an open round, X has 0 closed rounds, and across all rounds of X there are 0 DO entry headers (lines starting with `#### ` between the `### DO` line and the `### CHECK` line) | To Do |
| 2 | X has an open round | In Progress |
| 3 | X has 0 rounds and X = `#0` | To Do |
| 4 | X has 0 rounds | Undetermined |
| 5 | `Conclusion` of the latest closed round = Discarded | Canceled |
| 6 | Result of the latest closed round = Undetermined | Undetermined |
| 7 | Result of the latest closed round = Success | Done |
| 8 | `Conclusion` of the latest closed round = Pivot | On Hold |
| 9 | `Distance to destination` word of the latest closed round = Closer | In Progress |
| 10 | `Distance to destination` word of the latest closed round = Same or Farther | Blocked |
| 11 | Otherwise | Undetermined |

- ★ `Status:` = the status of the ★ `Attempt #:` attempt. `Result` of a Recent Attempts row = the result of the latest closed round of that attempt, `Conclusion` = the `Conclusion:` line value of that round. `/pdca-wrap` copies the `node .claude/hooks/nav.js state {Attempt PK}` output, and I-20 compares the written values with the computed values.
- A next direction candidate line (no attempt number) corresponds to Backlog. This value is written nowhere. The fact that the line is in the candidate list is that status.
- Item lines · `Distance to destination` format → grep -F "anchor:other-files-fk-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS) · Result, conclusion, status and distance vocabulary → grep -F "anchor:enum-column-vocab" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
