<!-- anchor:candidate-format -->
**Next direction candidate format** (`01_exploration_tree.md`)

- Candidate line = a line starting with `- ` in the "Next Direction Candidates" section. 0 or more lines and at most the count cap. With no candidates, no line is kept. Count cap → grep -F "anchor:01-format-position-path-attempt" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
- Candidate line regex (exact match): `^- \*\*[A-C]\.\*\* .+ — Branch point: {Attempt PK} — Basis: .+$` — in order: one of the bullets `A`·`B`·`C`, direction prose, the `Branch point:` value, basis prose. ({Attempt PK} → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS))
- `Branch point:` = the ★ `Attempt #:` value at the time the candidate is written.
- An attempt number is issued at the time the candidate is run. It is not issued in advance on the candidate line.
- When a candidate is run it moves to Recent Attempts as a row with a new number; when discarded without running it moves to Discarded Directions as a row with `#` = `—`; the candidate line is erased. `Branch point` value → grep -F "anchor:branch-point-value-rule" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
