**01 index format — ★ Current Position · Path · Recent Attempts · ◎ Best Record · count caps**

The format tests of `01_exploration_tree.md`. The single source of the format rules is here.

**Format 1 — ★ Current Position section** (source of I-01 count and line count · I-07 path and attempt #)
- Section header = a line matching `^## ★ Current Position`. **exactly 1 section** (I-01 section count).
- Body = the code fence block right after the header, **exactly 6 lines** inside (I-01 line count).
- 2 lines referenced by C3: `^Attempt #: {Attempt PK}$` · `^Path: .+$` ({Attempt PK} regex → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS); path value → Format 2).
- The other 4 lines (Direction, Status, Started, Body) count only toward the I-01 line count and are not format-tested by this block.
- Valid example: 1 `## ★ Current Position` + 6 lines · Violation examples: 2 headers (I-01 count violation) · a body of 5 or 7 lines (line count violation).

**Format 2 — Path** (source of I-07 both ends · I-08 end-1 and node count)
- path value := the value of the `Path:` line of the ★ section.
- nodes := the ordered sequence from splitting the path value by separator ` → ` (space + `→` + space). Each node = {Attempt PK} (regex → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)).
- I-07: `nodes[0] = #0` ∧ `nodes[end] = ★ Attempt #: value`.
- I-08: `|nodes| = 1 → skipped` · `|nodes| ≥ 2 → nodes[end-1] = Branch point of the current attempt` (Format 3).
- Valid example: `#0 → #4 → #11` · Violation examples: `#0->#4` (no spaces in the separator) · `#4 → #11` (first node ≠ #0).

**Format 3 — Recent Attempts table** (source of I-08 branch point · I-09 # and branch point)
- Header = `^\| # \| Branch point \| Direction \| Result \| Conclusion \| Lesson \| Body \|$`.
- Data row: `#` column = {Attempt PK} · `Branch point` column ∈ { {Attempt PK}, `—` }. `—` is allowed only in the row whose `#` column is `#0`, and `None` is forbidden.
- I-08: the `Branch point` column value of the current attempt (★ Attempt #) row.
- I-09: the integer comparison `Branch point ≤ #` in every data row (`#N` → N; rows whose `Branch point` column is `—` are left out of the comparison).
- Valid example: `| #11 | #4 | … |` (4 ≤ 11) · Violation examples: a Branch point cell of `None` (outside the vocabulary) · blank · `| #4 | #11 | … |` (11 ≤ 4 is false = I-09 order reversal).

**Format 4 — ◎ Best Record section** (I-02 count and line count)
- Section header = a line matching `^## ◎ Best Record`. **exactly 1 section** (I-02 section count).
- Body = the code fence block right after the header, **exactly 3 lines** inside (I-02 line count): `Closest attempt:` · `Why closest:` · `What blocked it:`.
- The value formats of the three lines count only toward the I-02 line count and are not tested by this format — value formats of the three lines → grep -F "anchor:01-field-format-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS) (after loading the block, scan the "◎ Best Record" rows).
- Valid example: 1 `## ◎ Best Record` + 3 lines · Violation examples: 2 headers (count violation) · a body of 2 or 4 lines (line count violation).

**Format 5 — section count caps** (I-03 · row count)
- Data row count cap of each section: `Return Log` ≤ 3 · `Recent Attempts` ≤ 3 · `Next Direction Candidates` ≤ 3.
- Test = the data row count of each section is at most the cap. Valid example: 3 Recent Attempts rows · Violation example: 4 Recent Attempts rows.
