**`00_destination.md` writing and editing rules**

- Who writes: body = `/pdca-init`, checkbox `[ ]`/`[x]` = `/pdca-wrap`. No other command writes this file.
- Structure = the structure template. Destination structure template → grep -F "anchor:00-file-structure" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
- Fixed line regex: `^(#|>|---$|\| Date \||\|-)` — a line this regex catches is a fixed line (titles, guidance lines, dividers, the two table header lines). The list of the fixed lines of the file gathered from the top must equal the fixed line list of the structure template character for character (trailing spaces are not compared). Fixed lines are not erased, edited or added.
- Item line regex (exact match): `^- \[( |x)\] \*\*({Destination criterion PK})\*\* — (.+)$` ({Destination criterion PK} → grep -F "anchor:pk-definition-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS))
- Placeholder line = a line of the structure template that is not a fixed line and contains `{`. If the file has even one line equal to a placeholder line, it is a violation.
- Value line = a line that is neither a fixed line nor a blank line. No value line is put above the first `## ` line. Value line condition per section:

| Section | Value line condition |
|---|---|
| `## Final Goal` | Exactly 1 line. One sentence that states the goal with a verb (e.g. `Build a 3D map of the factory as a digital twin in Isaac Sim and have the robot perform autonomous path finding`) |
| `## Success Criteria` | Only pairs of an item line placed below a `### ` line and the `In effect:` line directly below it. 1 or more pairs. Quantitative criterion = a criterion with a number and a way to measure it, qualitative criterion = a criterion a person judges by looking at the state |
| `## Constraints (must be kept)` | All start with `- `, and 1 or more lines. `- None` when checked and not applicable |
| `## Not the Destination (out of scope)` | All start with `- `, and 1 or more lines. `- None` when checked and not applicable |
| `## Destination Change History` | Table rows only. 1 or more data rows, and the `Change` and `Reason for change` cells are neither blank nor `—` |

- `{today}` = the `Today:` value of the `node .claude/hooks/nav.js dest` output.
- Numbers: the number of a new criterion = the `NextCriterionNumber` value of the `dest` output (the greatest existing number + 1 · discarded criteria included). Existing numbers are not changed or reused. Item line format and number condition → grep -F "anchor:other-files-fk-table" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
- Initial writing: the distribution has no `00_destination.md`. When the `dest` output is `DestinationFile: None`, create the file with `node .claude/hooks/nav.js dest --create` (the structure template is not copied by hand). Replace the placeholder lines of that file with value lines as in the table below and do not touch the other lines. Replace the template row of the change history with `| {today} | Initial version | None |`.

| Placeholder line | Number of approved values | How to write |
|---|---|---|
| `{Final goal in one sentence}` | 1 | Replace that line with the value line |
| The placeholder item line of each of the `### Quantitative criteria` section and the `### Qualitative criteria` section | 1 or more | In the place of the placeholder item line and the `In effect:` line directly below, write for each value a pair of a `- [ ] **D{number}** — {criterion}` line and a `      In effect: Valid` line, in the approved order |
| The placeholder item line of each of the `### Quantitative criteria` section and the `### Qualitative criteria` section | 0 | Erase the placeholder item line and the `In effect:` line directly below. Keep the `### ` line |
| Each of the `- {constraint}` line and the `- {out-of-scope item}` line | 1 or more | In the place of that line, write a `- {value}` line for each value, in the approved order |
| Each of the `- {constraint}` line and the `- {out-of-scope item}` line | 0 | Replace that line with `- None` |

- Numbers at initial writing: the first item of the quantitative section is `D1`, growing by 1 from top to bottom, and the first item of the qualitative section continues with the next number. The numbers written on the placeholder lines are not used. A destination with 0 quantitative and qualitative criteria in total is not written.
- An edit is one of the six below, and nothing else. For each edit, add a `| {today} | {Change} | {Reason for change} |` row at the very bottom of the change history.

| Edit | How to write | `Change` cell |
|---|---|---|
| Change the final goal | Replace the value line of `## Final Goal` with the new sentence | `Final Goal changed` |
| Add a criterion | At the very bottom of the section the user picked, quantitative or qualitative, add a `- [ ] **D{new number}** — {criterion}` line and an `In effect: Valid` line | `D{new number} added` |
| Discard a criterion | Change only the `In effect:` line of that criterion to `Discarded — {today}, {reason}`. Leave the item line as it is | `D{number} discarded` |
| Change the wording of a recorded criterion | Done as discard a criterion + add a criterion. The wording of the item line is not edited (the same goes for typo fixes) | `D{number} discarded, D{new number} added` |
| Change the wording of an unrecorded criterion | Change only the wording after ` — ` of that item line | `D{number} wording changed` |
| Change constraints or out-of-scope | Add, erase or change a `- ` line of that section | `Constraints changed` or `Out-of-scope changed` |

- Recorded criterion = a criterion with `Recorded` on its `Criterion:` line of the `dest` output (its number is in a full text of `00_destination.md` in `history/`). A criterion with `Unrecorded` is not yet in any history entry.
- Wording fixed condition → grep -F "anchor:invariant-table-T2" (NOTATION_CONVENTIONS)
